{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"classification\":\"blocker\",\"summary\":\"The documentation largely satisfies the provider, pipeline, release-note, and unchanged-file requirements, but it gives contradictory live-eval resume behavior and therefore does not consistently document the implemented checkpoint rule.\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"checkpoint-mismatch-behavior\",\"severity\":\"blocker\",\"summary\":\"README and RUNBOOK disagree about what happens when an explicitly resumed checkpoint is incompatible.\",\"evidence\":\"README.md says that for a report-format, contract-version, model, stage, or saved-selection mismatch, “any mismatch starts a fresh run.” RUNBOOK.md instead says such a mismatch “is refused rather than silently continued.” These are materially different operator-visible behaviors, and the latter is presented as the behavior of the `evals/live.py` referent.\",\"required_change\":\"Make both documents describe the actual `evals/live.py` behavior consistently. If an incompatible `--resume` is rejected, replace the README claim that it starts a fresh run with an explicit statement that resume is refused and that the operator must initiate a separate fresh run.\",\"regression\":false}]}"}}
